\ ff-test: lines
\ A `{ }` scope's barrier never outlives the word that raised it, and
\ `clear` / `depth` respect it.
\
\ An error inside a scope used to leave the barrier up for good: the
\ caller's cells stayed out of reach until ff_abort. `clear` inside a
\ scope emptied the whole stack - the caller's cells and the scope's own
\ inputs - which the closing `}` then slid down with a negative length.

: p 32 emit . ;
: eat { ( a -- b ) drop drop } ;
1 2 eat
drop drop depth . cr
: wipe { ( a -- ... ) 5 6 clear 7 } ;
1 2 3 wipe p p p cr
: count { ( a b -- n ) 9 depth nip } ;
10 20 30 count p p cr
